<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bessi</span></b> , ōrum, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βέσσοι</span>, Strab.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βησσοί</span>, Herod., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a savage and marauding people in the
				north-eastern part of Thrace</i>, <i>about the
				Hœmus mountains</i>, <i>and in the
				vicinity of the Hebrus</i>, <i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 2,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11,
				18, § 40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Pis.
				34, 84</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 3, 10, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 1,
			67</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 9, 2,
				91</span></i>.—<i>Sing.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bessus</span></b> , i,
			m., <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3548</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">3552</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bessĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of the Bessi</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 34, 84</span></i>
			.</div>
